    "function": "Toxic component of a type II toxin-antitoxin (TA) system. The cognate antitoxin is PhoAT; expression in M.smegmatis (strain mc(2)155) requires the cognate M.tuberculosis antitoxin gene. Expression in M.smegmatis strain mc(2)155 of the toxin alone slows growth and reduces cell viability, effects which are abrogated when cognate antitoxin PhoAT is coexpressed. Unwinds and/or cleaves 5'-tailed RNA in vitro that starts with 5'-AC, the reaction requires hydrolyzable ATP; double-stranded (ds)RNA and dsDNA are not unwound or cleaved. Can be expressed in the absence of its antitoxin gene in E.coli. In",
